# pulse — Docker build context trimmer (shared by Dockerfile + Dockerfile.web).
#
# Build context is `projects/pulse/`. Both images run their own isolated
# `pnpm install` inside the build, so committed node_modules / build outputs /
# local env / test + review surfaces are dead weight (and a security risk for
# .env). Keep ONLY what the stages COPY: server/{src,scripts,drizzle,*.json,
# *.config.*}, web/{src,public,*.json,*.config.*}, the umbrella manifests, the
# entrypoint, and the Dockerfiles themselves.

# --- dependencies (each stage installs its own) ---
**/node_modules

# --- build outputs ---
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- env + secrets (NEVER ship .env into an image) ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# --- local data / docker ---
docker-compose.yml
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# --- tests, review artifacts, coverage (not needed at runtime/build) ---
e2e
**/coverage
**/.review
**/__screenshots__
**/playwright-report
**/test-results

# --- docs + meta (the runtime never reads these) ---
PLAN.md
DECISIONS.md
PROGRESS.md
AGENT_NOTES.md
CHANGELOG.md
README.md
DEPLOY.md
*.md
.github

# --- editor / OS noise ---
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# --- git ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
